# Noctis: the technical one, in a maze of buttes. A plunge off a mesa into a square hairpin
# (two tight right-handers) around its tip, a chicane in its shadow, a steep climb onto a butte
# for a U-turn 16 m up, a long descent onto a dirt section of square hairpins (gently banked, no
# whoops), then a climb onto a last butte to a kicker: the landing hill bends one cell to the
# left under the flight (a "Tetris" jump: drift a little left in the air, land straight) and runs
# out onto the finish. Tight 90° turns everywhere; the speed comes from the drops.
name Noctis
seed 1971
# 2: smooth dirt, the whoops replaced by a straight. 3: the kicker and its shifted landing to the
# finish, instead of a climb into a 90° left and a plunge.
version 3
start 0 0 3 0
slope3_down3
turn1_right
straight
turn1_right
straight2
turn1_left
turn1_right
slope3_up2
turn1_left
checkpoint
turn1_left
slope3_down2
turn1_right
to_dirt
straight dirt
berm1_right dirt
straight2 dirt
berm1_left dirt
straight dirt
berm1_left dirt
checkpoint dirt
straight3 dirt
berm1_left dirt
to_road
turn1_right
checkpoint
slope3_up2
kicker
kicker_landing5_down2_left
finish

terrain hills 10.0
terrain relief 18.0
# The start mesa, 24 m, stretched along the plunge so it runs down a cutting, with a spur of rock
# between the plunge and the road back; the cliffs to the west of it.
landform mesa 10 50 34 34 110 0
landform butte 150 80 45 64
landform butte 60 -95 30 40
# The butte of the U-turn, 16 m: both of its roads climb and drop through slots cut into it. A
# needle between them and a wall to the south.
landform mesa -112 -32 56 24 60 0
landform butte -112 10 12 34
landform mesa -122 -222 60 52 220 90
# Around the dirt section.
landform butte -192 -42 16 28
landform butte -367 -92 20 38
landform butte -377 138 16 30
landform mesa -462 28 50 46 280 0
# The last butte, 16 m, under the climb to the kicker. The jump flies over open ground, rock
# kept well clear of the landing on both sides; an escarpment closes the view past the finish.
landform mesa -240 200 44 24 60 0
landform butte -130 310 22 30
landform mesa -60 280 45 42
landform butte 40 210 25 36
landform mesa -370 298 45 50 160 20
landform mesa -200 760 55 55 300 90
# Hoodoos and boulders: in the island of the dirt hairpins, beyond them, below the start mesa,
# around the last butte (hiding the foot of its climb from the dirt), beside the jump and at the
# finish.
prop spire -272 0 30 20 6
prop rock -270 0 4 75 2.5
prop spire -300 0 -112 10 9
prop spire -318 0 -98 140 6
prop boulder -284 0 -126 60 7
prop boulder -92 0 104 30 7
prop rock -100 0 92 200 2.5
prop spire -118 0 222 15 8
prop spire -104 0 242 100 5
prop boulder -274 0 156 40 10
prop slab -273 0 180 300 7
prop spire -292 0 340 30 7
